-## What the match can establish
+## Preserve the scope and metadata differences
 
-The Interim Report appears to belong to the draft text Hyde reviewed. The full clause matches across the visible page images, and searching the 56 page-level OCR files after joining whitespace gave one page hit, physical p. 31. That search measures the retrieved OCR only. It cannot distinguish byte-identical attachments or versions that share the clause.
+- The **October 14** certification and the roster exceptions stand side by side. The roster gives no proof of later contact for the three p. 3 exceptions. The **October 16** certification has a different visible population. Do not use the three-person return as confirmation of the Regional Office roster. The travel-or-leave column shows **9/11/01** on AGL-6 p. 3 and **9/11/03** on p. 5. Both pages identify the employee population with **9/11/01** in their main headings. The column readings remain unresolved.
+- The catalogue reports object sizes of **489,232** bytes for AGL-2 and **100,934** for AGL-4. The linked PDF bodies returned **1,052,468** and **156,104** bytes respectively. AGL-6 reports and returned **2,580,396** bytes. Preserve the catalogue fields and retrieved body lengths. The source of the differences and any edition relationship remain untested.
+- Commission staff's October 8 account of what managers reported about earlier requests, FAA's October 14 possible-incompleteness warning, and the later OIG's finding of no indication of intentional withholding have separate scopes. The new records add headquarters instructions and specific regional returns. They leave the cause of any omission and the adequacy of the full production open. [Prior source comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/8c169cde263a06e82f18bc69742430f540101402/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-october-tasking-records-2026-11-05/README.md) · [DOT OIG CC-2004-003, p. 2](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2004003.pdf#page=2)
 
-The file preserves a planned front-office circulation, an undated candidate report addressed to commissioners and the front office, and draft accounts of forwarding and limits on further staff investigation. Keep **“Permission was denied”** and **“staff was advised not to pursue this avenue”** as separate accounts. The compared passages leave the signed decision, decision maker, exact recipients and relationship between the two reported instructions unresolved. The April 22 circulation and deferral recollections remain distinct. The June 7/June 9 date discrepancy and June 8 planned distribution remain unresolved. [April 22 recollections](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/5fe51e466b12474ae2f69d6e7f449b341d8bd6f0/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-referral-memo-distribution-2026-11-05/README.md) · [June agenda and version comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0d9f2479de37c210734dec68b9b5d0ef96553302/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-june8-agenda-transmittal-2026-11-08/README.md)
